From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove@yandex.ru>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:33:50 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 137/297] Meridian: any tab can be renamed, and a double click
 does it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rename… was in a pinned tab's menu only. A Today tab has it now, and a
double click on a tab, a pinned tab or a folder puts its name in a field in
place (Arc): Return keeps it, Escape doesn't.

A Today tab's name is the tab's own (TabData, saved with the session as tab
extra data, so it is there after a restart and comes back with a reopened
tab); the sidebar's page gets it with the tab's space. No name gives the
page's title back. Pinned, the tab takes the name to its item. The names
Tidy Today gives are kept the same way: they used to be lost on a restart.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
